<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bulolo</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Bulolo is a town in Morobe Province, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/papua-new-guinea">Papua New Guinea</a>, in the valley of the Bulolo River. Gold was found in the area in the 1920s, and in the 1930s huge dredges were flown in piece by piece from Lae, a landmark in the history of air freight. After gold mining declined the town became a centre of forestry and plywood production.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/bulolo.jpg" alt="Bulolo" width="320" height="273" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Photograph: NASA · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bulolo.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
